WEBVTT

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:48.480
Hmm?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.650
Don't you think it's strange not to realize

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:59.990
that the limits of the leader's abilities
place a limit on the team's abilities?

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.610
You understand that, don't you?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.580
Yeah, of course.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.120
It's a shame that nobody understands

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.370
what I tell them.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.500
It's outrageous, isn't it?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.960
I can't stand to play with
those people anymore!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.160
You can't touch tar without
getting your hands dirty.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:19.700
What do I do?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.760
Although, they have
their cases to make, too.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.050
Hey...!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.250
What I'm saying isn't getting
through to you, either.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.150
What gives, you...!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:37.990
Wait!

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.970
Wait?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.300
I see.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.200
You, too, must be...

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.060
...my enemy!

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.870
What? What about you?!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.960
I'd like to do something for her.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.270
"Look out! Get out of the way!!"

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:17.500
We're not playing with you, Haruto!

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.920
Haruto, you're a drag.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.040
You're bugging us.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.630
Haruto, you're a drag!

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:23.420
You're bothering us!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.090
--I thought you were a 
little smarter than that.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.800
--I thought you were a little smarter than that.
--I thought you were a little smarter than that.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:28.970
Huh?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.090
(Thank goodness you came to!)

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.130
(Are you all right?)

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.760
(Eh?)

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:41.920
(Are you o

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:42.960
kay?)

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.340
(Huh?)

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.570
Two witches have appeared?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.030
That's nice and glamorous, isn't it?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.570
That's true,

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:14.870
but one of them has a strong
personality, and is aggressive.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.080
You like strong young ladies, don't you?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.500
Huh?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.010
She may be more at the end
of her rope than you think.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.640
Why don't you offer her

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.280
a sympathetic ear to talk to?

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:33.500
So, what about the other one?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.260
Ah, I didn't get to talk to her.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.630
I couldn't hear her.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.910
Ah, come to think of it...

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.770
You couldn't hear her?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.280
Nor the other sounds around you?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.780
No. I'm not sure whether or not
she could hear <i>my</i> voice, either.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:01.000
The two of you need to find some
other means of communication,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.580
is that what you mean?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.710
(Are you all right?)

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.510
You say he can't converse
with someone in a dream?

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.320
What's up with that?

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.770
That's what I'm asking you.

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:27.270
A dream is a sort of world
of thought, right?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:31.560
Maybe they're on such different
wavelengths that they can't talk.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.230
If they're meeting in a dream, I'd say their

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:37.660
wavelengths are pretty close.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.290
Hmm?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:43.570
Ah...

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:59.100
That lady just now...

00:08:59.100 --> 00:08:59.850
Huh?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.450
Deaf Vocal?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.990
Excuse me, what is Deaf Vocal?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:36.180
<i>A bright parade of light</i>
<i>in the colors of the rainbow</i>

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:41.970
<i>You can cry, but your tears</i>
<i>will stream across the sky</i>

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:47.730
<i>Leaving a trail of light</i>
<i>in the colors of the rainbow</i>

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:52.270
<i>You can color me with it too</i>

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:56.490
<i>The color of the future</i>

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.390
Ah...

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.090
Deaf Vocal...

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.820
...is a band for the deaf?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.400
<i>You’re so precious, I’m just so happy</i>

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:37.150
<i>I can’t even put it into words</i>

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:42.450
<i>When you smile like the sun</i>

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:49.920
<i>Everything becomes a joy to me</i>

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.970
She sings in sign language?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:04.430
You could say that the energy
of her thoughts are contained in it.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:07.430
The energy... of her thoughts?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.690
Her hearing impairment could
be due to a lot of things,

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.400
whether she was born with it
or had some illness,

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.300
but she's doing her best, every day.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.190
"Raw Noodle Prince: The Movie"

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.540
I've been in the rubble for a whole week,

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.690
and nobody's even realized it!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:56.540
Oh...

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:01.330
Are you deaf?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.050
Yes, at least in the real world.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.220
But in this world?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.430
No problem.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.490
You can hear?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.180
Not so much hear

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.440
as I can clearly understand what you say.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.560
Even if I don't look at your mouth.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.770
Look at my mouth?

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:24.900
Yeah. In this world,
I can freely say anything I think,

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.030
I can convey anything
about myself that I please,

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.280
and I can listen to others unimpeded.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.820
It allows what I want to come true.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:37.290
Look at you--you're taking
the form that you want, right?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.060
Huh?

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:41.950
You don't want to wake up from this dream.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.800
Somewhere, in your feelings,
that's what you're thinking.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.800
N-No way.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.680
I'm going to wake up soon,

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.500
and do all sorts of things
I want to back in that world.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.440
What is it you want to do?

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.710
Well, I...

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.560
Is it something that you can only do in the
other world, where you were before?

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.700
Then that's another matter,
for when you're <i>there</i>.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.620
You just need to do whatever you can <i>here</i>.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.700
What I can do here?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.080
You're already doing it,
aren't you? Spontaneously?

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:23.960
You're here taking in my griping,
my bitching, my whining and my abuse.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.500
Well, that's because...

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.840
that's what I sensed your heart
was wanting to shout out.

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.060
Even so,

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.350
you're the only one who was able hear them.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.980
Huh? What do you mean?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:43.110
That no one else besides me
could hear what you say?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:45.540
Yes. Right, Mr. Cat?

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:51.380
Huh? You couldn't hear what she was saying?

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.540
Who'd willingly want to listen to the
negative things a stranger is saying?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:00.050
People unconsciously choose to hear
only the sounds that suit them.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:05.280
That's why, depending on the person,
others can't hear what I say.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.550
Does that mean...

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.180
You've experienced it in
this world, too, haven't you?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.050
Me? In this world?

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:15.560
Yes.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.100
<i>You</i> weren't able to hear her voice, were you?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.810
My <i>other</i> voice?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.070
Another you?

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.110
Who, her?

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:31.110
You can have everything you
want here in the dream world,

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.070
so why?

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.660
I already told you.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.100
We take the forms that we want to.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.500
That's what this is?

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.500
That can't be right!

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.630
I want to hear everything,
and besides, I want to help others.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:49.730
Mm-hmm, you've helped me plenty.
Both me, and others, I'm sure.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.720
But the one you really want to help...

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.850
...is you, yourself, isn't it?

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.800
Me... myself?

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.060
Yes. You, yourself

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.900
want to help <i>you</i>, don't you?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.150
Not want to <i>be</i> helped...

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.900
...but want to help.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.660
I want to help myself?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:19.570
I've never even thought of that.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:26.030
But there isn't any way 
for me to help myself.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.250
That's why you have <i>others</i>, isn't it?

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:31.170
Huh?

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:32.170
Huh?

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:36.300
Up to now, lots of others have
wanted to be helped by you,

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.930
and have approached you.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:42.480
And you also naturally attract them.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.620
I do?

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:49.070
You took what they said, which you'd
ordinarily refuse to listen to,

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:50.780
and accepted it.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:56.450
On the other hand, you don't accept
the things that give you courage,

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.580
or cheer you up, so you don't hear them.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.580
Huh? I can't hear when
others cheer me on?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.080
That can't be right, can it?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.950
Somewhere in there, you're thinking,
"little old me," aren't you?

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.130
Self-deprecatingly?

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.120
Because I don't accept it?

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.640
You were surprised when
you learned I was in a band

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.510
even though I can't hear, weren't you?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.010
To be honest...

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.580
Still, I want to sing.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.390
I want to act, too.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.480
And walk the runway!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.840
If you heard that, now 
would you laugh it off,

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:52.990
telling me "That's not possible for you"?

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.880
You couldn't do that, huh?

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:00.950
I mean, you already know that
it isn't impossible for me.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.610
It's not as though everyone
leads the same life as you do.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:11.320
But if you realize that
even a little bit, I'd be glad.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:15.320
I'd also be glad if the anime
and movies that I love had subtitles.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.180
Yeah.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.300
Glad?

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.320
Yeah.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:21.330
Yeah.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:25.200
By learning the slightest
bit about someone...

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.000
...by changing your
point of view just a bit...

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.340
...your feelings toward that person
suddenly grow a lot closer.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.750
Getting to know them;

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:36.840
listening for their voice...

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:43.390
Just by opening up the doorway
to your heart a little wider,

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.960
you change.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.100
I'm glad I...

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:29.560
Huh?

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.400
I'm glad I...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.900
I'm glad I met you!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:47.190
Huh? Huh...?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:50.250
I'll see you later!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:53.670
Huh?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.770
She sure was a preachy little lady, huh?

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:19.690
Whether she sounded preachy or not...

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:23.490
...just depends on if you open
the doorway to your heart a little wider...

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.580
...doesn't it?

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:39.000
According to the American psychologist,
Dr. Albert Mehrabian,

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.470
the input we receive from
communication with others

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.760
is 55 percent facial expressions,

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:49.390
38 percent vocal pitch, loudness, and speed,

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.480
while the meaning of the
words that are spoken...

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:55.480
...accounts for a mere seven percent.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:58.150
Oh yeah, that low?

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.940
It's not just our words;

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.990
we need to realize the
importance of communication.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:08.830
Like how a person's feelings
are directly reproduced

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:12.420
in the range of an analog record
that people can't hear.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:15.000
By the way...

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.590
Why did you bring that guitar with you?

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:21.420
Oh, I went to a live music club
for the first time in a while,

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.010
and it made me want to play.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:30.520
Jeez, keep the sound off
until you've finished tuning.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:36.520
I can't tune it unless
there's sound, you know.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:41.530
It's not until a person's heart
produces the sound of their actions

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.530
that they can start tuning, either.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.030
Still, you have to cut out
the sounds that interfere with it.

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:33.890
Would you like to know what
your favorite idol is really like?

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:36.270
Yes I would, baa!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:41.440
"Idols Don't
Go to the Bathroom!"

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:41.440
Next time's dream is
"Idols Don't Go to the Bathroom!"
